WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.620
After a fast-paced season 7, the Long Night
of waiting for Game of Thrones Season eight

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.840
is upon us, and according to actor Kit Harrington,
the final season is going to be an absolute

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.840
bloodbath!

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.600
A lot has happened over the course of the
last seven seasons, including the deaths of

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.830
over 200 named characters… which has me
wondering whose neck will end up on the proverbial

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.259
chopping block next season.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:26.570
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm predicting the characters likely

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.980
to die in the epic final season of Game of
Thrones.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.110
I'm also starting a new Funko Pop giveaway.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.880
All you have to do is be a subscriber to my
channel and leave a comment on this video

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.290
for a chance to win.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.480
Quick spoiler warning, I'll be reviewing major
character arcs from all seven seasons so far,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.440
so take care if you're not caught up.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.760
Let's kick off with one of the characters
many of us love to hate on Game of Thrones:

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.170
Cersei Lannister.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.410
Back in season 5, Maggy the Frog made a number
of predictions for Cersei which have come

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.900
true, including the death of her three children
so far.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.250
However, George RR Martin's books include
another prophecy by Maggy that Cersei will

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.280
be choked to death by the valonqar, which
is High Valyrian for 'little brother', or

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.560
possibly 'little sister' or 'little sibling.'

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.700
So, could this mean that we'll see Tyrion
strangle Cersei, just like he did his former

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.700
lover Shae?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.429
I don't know if it'll be that simple.

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:17.850
After all, Jaime Lannister may be Cersei's
twin, but he's actually slightly younger than

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:18.850
her.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:22.659
Season 7 has already teased Jaime as a possible
valonqar, for example, there's the scene which

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:27.259
showed Cersei and Jaime standing on a huge
map of Westeros, with Cersei at the area called

00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:30.249
the neck and Jaime by the area known as the
fingers.

00:01:30.249 --> 00:01:34.369
And the two are now estranged after she accused
him of treason when he chose to ride north

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:39.579
after she reneged on her agreement to unite
with Dany and Jon against the White Walkers.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:44.020
And remember Euron Greyjoy's reply to Cersei's
accusation that he killed his own brother:

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.759
'You should try it,' Euron said, 'it feels
wonderful.'

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:51.540
So, to prevent the prophecy or because she
feels they've betrayed her, will Cersei attempt

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.939
to follow through on her threats to kill her
brothers, yet end up hoist by her own petard?

00:01:56.939 --> 00:02:01.369
Also, with each passing day, Cersei seems
to act more and more like a mix of her father

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:04.389
Tywin and the Mad King Aerys Targaryen.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:09.250
The thing is: Tywin was killed by Tyrion and
Jaime reluctantly killed the Mad King to prevent

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:14.051
him from carrying out his crazy plan of setting
the whole of King's Landing on fire, so it

00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:17.989
wouldn't be beyond belief if either of them
found themselves in a similar position with

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:18.989
Cersei.

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:23.260
Yet, Jaime and Tyrion aren't the only characters
who could fulfil the valonqar prophecy.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.490
Among other potential Cersei assassins is
Arya, who hasn't had a chance to cross the

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:31.650
Mad Queen off her kill-list yet for her part
in Ned Stark's death.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:37.409
Ok, totally crazy theory time now: What if
Arya got hold of the decapitated dwarf head

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:42.319
that looked like Tyrion and which Qyburn took
to use for his work in Season 5?

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.569
She could then take its face and choke Cersei
as a Tyrion look-a-like, in a similar stunt

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:49.730
to the one she pulled on Walder Frey's men
at the start of season 7.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:55.370
Or what if Arya put Jaime to death for trying
to kill her brother Bran back in season 1,

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.020
and then she used Jaime's face to fulfil the
prophecy?

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.870
Or Arya could make use of the newly deceased
Littlefinger's face to slip back into Cersei's

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:07.530
court under the pretence of providing her
with intel on her northern enemies.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.590
Another character that many of us are probably
itching to see get his just desserts before

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:17.159
the series is over is Gregor Clegane, aka
Ser Robert Strong, the Undead Mountain.

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:21.409
It's been a long time coming, but after the
Hound's fighting words to his brother in the

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:25.819
Dragonpit, it certainly looks like they're
teasing Cleganebowl for season 8.

00:03:25.819 --> 00:03:29.750
For anyone who doesn't know, Cleganebowl is
the fan theory that the story arcs for the

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.329
two brothers Sandor and Gregor Clegane will
culminate in an epic face-off.

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:38.310
Now, on the surface, Gregor would appear to
have the upper hand against Sandor, being

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.280
larger, stronger and, most importantly now,
undead.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.849
But I feel the show has spent time thrusting
The Hound into situations where he's confronted

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:49.620
by flames, which he's scared of given his
childhood experience with fire.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.560
I think this may be foreshadowing a crucial
moment where he overcomes his fear which he'll

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.859
need to do to finally defeat the Mountain.

00:03:55.859 --> 00:04:00.430
I suspect that an ordinary weapon won't be
able to kill Ser Robert Strong, so Sandor

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.270
might do it with a dragonglass blade, or how
about this for a wild theory: Beric Dondarrion

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:09.290
could light The Hound's blade on fire and
the Hound could then use the flaming sword

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:14.840
to slice into his undead brother's face in
a moment of sweet symbolic revenge.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.830
Beric Dondarrion's status at the end of season
7 was uncertain as he was on top of the wall

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.970
as the ice dragon blasted a huge chunk of
the wall down.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.190
The last time we saw him and Tormund, though,
it looked like they were on the part of the

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.590
wall that was left standing.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:31.880
But I don't think the Lightning Lord will
make it through the whole of next season alive

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.450
as his death has been pretty heavily foreshadowed
in season seven.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:39.919
Now that his good friend and chief resurrecter
Thoros of Myr is dead, Beric is on his last

00:04:39.919 --> 00:04:40.919
life.

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:43.800
And Beric himself pointed out that the reason
he's been brought back from the dead is to

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.760
help kill the Walkers.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.580
What I think could happen is that Beric goes
in to battle expecting to kill the Night King

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:54.710
with a dragonglass or flaming Valyrian steel
blade, but it doesn't work on the icy sovereign.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.840
Beric will die heroically, but not completely
in vain as Jon Snow could witness the death

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.780
and realise that it will take something more
to kill the Night King.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.910
I really hope this doesn't happen, but I'm
fearful for our Onion Knight Davos Seaworth

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.060
next season.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.639
He's one of the few good-natured characters
on the show, having been loyal to the men

00:05:12.639 --> 00:05:16.750
he's served; he was a friend to Shireen Baratheon;
and he was instrumental in saving Gendry from

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.150
Melisandre and in bringing him back into the
story in season seven.

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:24.510
But, when he said recently that "all [he'd]
ever done was live to a ripe old age", I immediately

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.280
thought "oh, oh", are the writers planning
to brutally kill him off?

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.140
I really hope that's not what lies ahead for
Davos, but it does feel like his character

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.819
arc could be coming to its natural end.

00:05:34.819 --> 00:05:38.940
There's one loose thread, though, which needs
resolution before we see Davos leave us, and

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.449
that's his threat to Melisandre back in Winterfell
that he would execute her if he ever saw her

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:44.940
again.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.060
This brings us to the Red Woman herself, who
departed Westeros this season in her usual

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:54.250
cryptic manner, but gave a few clues to her
future when she spoke to Varys on Dragonstone.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.889
During the conversation, Melisandre said she
was leaving for Volantis but that she had

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:03.020
to return to Westeros one last time where,
she added mysteriously, that she would die.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.069
The thing with Melisandre, though, is that
she's extremely hard to kill – she's over

00:06:06.069 --> 00:06:10.580
400 years old and has survived assassination
attempts like when Maester Cressen served

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.030
her poisoned wine in Season 2.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:17.490
For a hint at how she might peg it, let's
look back at her encounter with Arya in Season

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:18.980
3 where this happened.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.680
"I see a darkness in you."

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.740
"And in that darkness eyes staring back at
me..."

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.550
"We will meet again."

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:31.050
And let's not forget either that Melisandre
is still on Arya's kill-list.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:35.310
Arya now has a Valyrian steel dagger, which
could be enough to kill the Red Priestess

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:40.140
in season eight, but I think she'll also have
to remove Melisandre's magical choker first

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.420
as well.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:46.320
And remember that during Melisandre's conversation
with Varys, she also revealed that he too

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.139
had to die in Westeros.

00:06:48.139 --> 00:06:51.890
And that wasn't the first encounter we've
seen between Varys and a red priestess.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:56.130
Back in Meereen in season 6, Varys met with
Kinvara, who revealed she knew about the time

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:59.599
a sorcerer castrated him and cast his manhood
into the fire.

00:06:59.599 --> 00:07:04.010
Kinvara also knew about the voice that Varys
heard from the flames, which was presumably

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:09.340
the fate that lies ahead for him, and which
it looks like Melisandre also knows about.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.540
And there was some possible foreshadowing
of the fact that Varys will die, even if it's

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:16.699
not in this way, when Daenerys told him he
must stand up to her if he ever thought she

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:21.639
was failing as a ruler and that she would
burn him alive if she discovered he was betraying

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:22.639
her.

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:28.020
Moving on to the ironborn, I think Theon could
be a Greyjoy casualty in season 8.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:32.650
After abandoning his sister Yara during Euron's
attack in season seven, Theon wants to redeem

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.150
himself by launching a raid to rescue her.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:39.370
I can see the show having Theon successfully
free Yara, but there's a chance he might not

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.870
survive that final act of redemption.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:47.229
Alternately, Theon could survive and either
he or Yara could kill Euron during the rescue.

00:07:47.229 --> 00:07:51.360
That would be an interesting way to go as
it would put Yara back in charge of the Iron

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.360
Islands.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.419
Now, one character whose death could shock
a lot of fans and who I think has a chance

00:07:56.419 --> 00:07:58.849
of dying is Sansa Stark.

00:07:58.849 --> 00:08:03.030
Sansa's death could be a heart-breaking moment
for fans of the lemon-cake-loving Lady of

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:07.979
Winterfell, so what suggests the elder Stark
sister could kick the bucket before the series

00:08:07.979 --> 00:08:08.979
ends?

00:08:08.979 --> 00:08:10.129
Well, in a letter that George R.R.

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:14.349
Martin penned back in 1993, he revealed the
five characters he planned to survive the

00:08:14.349 --> 00:08:15.650
whole of his book series.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:20.830
Those lucky five were Daenerys Targaryen,
Arya Stark, Jon Snow, Bran Stark, and Tyrion

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:21.830
Lannister.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:26.080
If this original vision is something showrunners
Benioff and Weiss plan to stick to, it seems

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.830
that Sansa will not make it to the end.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.940
And something which could foreshadow Sansa's
eventual demise is the death of her direwolf

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.130
Lady back in season one.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:39.280
The Starks have all had strong connections
to their direwolves with only Jon and Arya's

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.789
direwolves still alive.

00:08:40.789 --> 00:08:45.260
Although Bran survived his direwolf's death,
you could argue that Summer died around the

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:49.570
time Bran lost his personal identity and became
the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:53.980
Sansa has been on quite a journey on the show,
progressing from a naïve young girl with

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:58.860
dreams of knights and princes to becoming
a more politically savvy operator in the North.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:02.890
To get to this point though she's been played,
betrayed and abused by various people from

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:06.870
Joffrey and Cersei to Littlefinger and Ramsay,
so you might wonder how on earth could the

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.650
TV show kill her off after all that?

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:14.610
Well, her death might not be as a helpless
victim, rather it could be heroic or noble

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.600
in some way, for example, defending the North
or Winterfell against a horde of invading

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.600
White Walkers.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:23.550
Then again, Sansa appeared to be displeased
about her brother Jon bending the knee to

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:28.110
Daenerys, so how will she react when he arrives
at Winterfell with Dany, and on top of that

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:32.100
what about when she discovers that he's also
a secret Targaryen?

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.610
Will she still treat Jon as one of the Stark
wolf pack?

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:39.600
I know that losing any of the characters I've
been talking about would be a big blow depending

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.000
on who your favourites are, but there's still
one really shocking death the showrunners

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.560
might decide to do late in the season.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.250
When talking about the ending he's planned
for his Song of Ice and Fire series, George

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.250
R.R.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.990
Martin has said that it will be "bittersweet"
and that "you can't just fulfil a quest and

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.040
then pretend life is perfect".

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:00.630
Which means that the hero or heroes we've
favoured are unlikely to get a perfectly happy

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:01.630
ending.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:06.490
So, although we will get some kind of satisfying
resolution, it will also be tinged with sadness.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:09.880
Which could mean that one of the two main
characters many fans have rooted for over

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:14.660
the seasons, Jon Snow or Daenerys Targaryen,
may have to sacrifice themselves to defeat

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.140
the Night King and his army.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:21.630
The season 7 finale has just paired up our
heroes, but the reveal of Jon's Targaryen

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:26.700
heritage could drive a wedge between the couple
if Dany thinks he's a threat to her claim.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.072
Alternately, Jon and Dany could continue to
work together to defeat the undead threat,

00:10:30.072 --> 00:10:34.980
and either Dany or Jon could be revealed to
be Azor Ahai or the Prince or Princess That

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.010
Was Promised.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:39.990
In the legend of Azor Ahai, the sword that
could defeat the Darkness could only be forged

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.640
when the hero drove it into the chest of his
beloved Nissa Nissa.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:47.760
And to fulfil that prophecy, Dany or Jon could
have to forge a new Lightbringer sword by

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.649
plunging it into the heart of their new love.

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:55.340
Still, George RR Martin said in the early
90s that Jon and Dany were two of five characters

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:59.420
who would make it to the end of his books,
and he also told the crew working on season

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.600
1 of the show that bringing Dany and Jon together
was the end game.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:07.240
So, if the showrunners do take the Azor Ahai
route, perhaps bringing Dany or Jon back from

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:11.279
the dead could be one of Melisandre's final
acts before her own demise.

00:11:11.279 --> 00:11:16.040
Now, I'd love to hear who you think will get
the chop and who will survive to the end of

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.040
Game of Thrones.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.630
And what are your predictions for the final
season?

